                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.20/169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-31T17:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. From the Under Secretary. Your 311, October 30, 6 p.m.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d434-f1"/> I have spoken this morning with the Bolivian Minister
                    regarding this question. He is communicating immediately with his Government and
                    is reminding them that a formal commitment to this Government was made in
                    writing covering the termination of the services of the Italian mission in
                    October 1941. The recommendations in your telegram will be given immediate
                    consideration. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
